# Online play.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill both values in. `.env.local` is
# ignored by git (`*.local`), which is the point: the anon key is safe to ship
# in a bundle but there is no reason to put a particular project's key in this
# repository.
#
# Leave both blank — or skip the file entirely — and the game still runs. The
# scenario screen simply says why the online buttons are dead, and every game is
# played here, exactly as it is today. Vite reads `VITE_`-prefixed variables
# only, and `src/main.ts` is the only file that reads any of them.
#
# Both come from the Supabase dashboard, under Project Settings -> API.

# The project's REST endpoint, e.g. https://abcdefghijklmnop.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# The *anon* key, never the service role key.
#
# The service role belongs to one participant and one only: the `game` Edge
# Function, which is the referee. It is the key that can write the command log,
# read the seed and see the whole board, and a browser holding it would be a
# player who could do all three. The anon key grants nothing on its own — the
# client signs in anonymously with it and row level security decides the rest.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the companion Ogre app lives, for the war room's "Open in the Ogre app"
# link on a ground battle.
#
# Optional, and only about that one link: every ground battle can be fought
# here instead, and is by default. It exists for forks, for local hacking, and
# for anybody who would rather fight the ground half on another machine.
# Unset, it falls back to https://onlinemph.github.io/OGRE-VTT/.
VITE_OGRE_URL=
